 Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.iso.org/standard/78925.html\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 173\nL0: cite0†Image L1: \nL2: Reference number\nL3: ISO/IEC 11179-31:2023\nL4: \nL5: © ISO 2026\nL6: \nL7: International Standard\nL8: \nL9: ISO/IEC 11179-31:2023\nL10: \nL11: Information technology — Metadata registries (MDR) — Part 31: Metamodel for data specification registration\nL12: \nL13: Edition 1\nL14: 2023-01\nL15: \nL16: Preview this standard in our Online Browsing Platform (OBP)\nL17: \nL18: [Button: Read sample]\nL19: \nL20: cite1†Published (Edition 1, 2023)\nL21: \nL22: ### ISO/IEC 11179-31:2023\nL23: \nL24: Language\nL25: \nL26: [Select]\nL27: \nL28: Format\nL29: \nL30: [Input] PDF + ePub\nL31: \nL32: [Input] Paper\nL33: \nL34: CHF (Swiss francs) 0\nL35: \nL36: [Button: Add to cart]\nL37: ### Preview ISO/IEC 11179-31:2023\nL38: ## Abstract\nL39: \nL40: This document provides a specification for an extension to a Metadata Registry (MDR), as specified in ISO/IEC 11179-3, in which metadata that describes data elements and associated concepts, such as “data element concepts”, “conceptual domains” and “value domains” can be registered.\nL41: \nL42: The specification in this document, together with the relevant clauses of the specification in ISO/IEC 11179-3, provides the ability to record metadata about:\nL43: a)    data elements, units of measure and derivation rules;\nL44: \nL45: b)    data element concepts and associated object classes and properties;\nL46: \nL47: c)    conceptual domains, conceptual domain subsets and value meanings;\nL48: \nL49: d)    value domains, value domain subsets, datatypes and permissible values.\nL50: This document is applicable to the formulation of data representations, concepts, meanings and relationships to be shared among people and machines, independent of the organization that produces the data. It is not applicable to the physical representation of data as bits and bytes at the machine level.\nL51: ## General information\nL52: \nL53:   * Status\nL54: \nL55:  : Published\nL56: \nL57: Publication date\nL58: \nL59:  : 2023-01\nL60: \nL61: Stage\nL62: \nL63: : International Standard published [cite1†60.60 ]\nL64: \nL65:   * Edition\nL66: \nL67:  : 1\nL68: \nL69: Number of pages\nL70: \nL71:  : 76\nL72: \nL73:   * Technical Committee :\nL74: \nL75: cite2†ISO/IEC JTC 1/SC 32 L76: \nL77: ICS :\nL78: \nL79: cite3†35.040.50 L80: \nL81:   * cite4†RSS updates\nL82: \nL83: ## Life cycle\nL84: \nL85:   * ### Now\nL86: \nL87: Published\nL88: #### ISO/IEC 11179-31:2023\nL89: \nL90: cite5†Stage: 60.60 L91: \nL92:     * 00\nL93: \nL94: Preliminary\nL95: \nL96:     * 10\nL97: \nL98: Proposal\nL99: \nL100:       * cite6†10.99 2019-07-03 New project approved L101:     * 20\nL102: \nL103: Preparatory\nL104: \nL105:     * 30\nL106: \nL107: Committee\nL108:       * cite7†30.00 2020-07-13 Committee draft (CD) registered L109:       * cite8†30.20 2020-07-14 CD consultation initiated L110:       * cite9†30.60 2020-09-09 Close of comment period L111:       * cite10†30.92 2021-02-26 CD referred back to Working Group L112:       * cite8†30.20 2021-02-26 CD consultation initiated L113:       * cite9†30.60 2021-04-24 Close of comment period L114:       * cite10†30.92 2021-08-23 CD referred back to Working Group L115:       * cite8†30.20 2021-08-23 CD consultation initiated L116:       * cite9†30.60 2021-10-20 Close of comment period L117:       * cite11†30.99 2022-01-25 CD approved for registration as DIS L118:     * 40\nL119: Enquiry\nL120: \nL121:       * cite12†40.00 2022-03-07 DIS registered L122:       * cite13†40.20 2022-05-09 DIS ballot initiated: 12 weeks L123:       * cite14†40.60 2022-08-02 Close of voting L124:       * cite15†40.99 2022-10-11 Full report circulated: DIS approved for registration as FDIS L125:     * 50\nL126: \nL127: Approval\nL128:       * cite16†50.00 2022-10-12 Final text received or FDIS registered for formal a